A compound statement in programming or logic refers to a statement that combines two or more statements into one larger statement. This can be useful for making code cleaner and easier to read.

For example:
```csharp
if (x > 0 && y < 10)
{
    // do something
}
```
This is a single line of code that does the same thing as two separate lines:

```csharp
if (x > 0) {
    if (y < 10) {
        // do something
    }
}
```

